From 9d12c0fecf5a65994553f3d87911a5446adb8466 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:53:42 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 225/235] Import: R14 DXF header says the drawing is metric
 ($MEASUREMENT 1)

The header had $INSUNITS 4 (mm), which R14 does not define. LibreDWG's dxf2dwg
ignores it for an AC1014 file, the DWG gets MEASUREMENT 0 (imperial), and
reading it back scaled everything by 25.4 (a circle of length 2159 came back
as 54848 after DWG export and import). $MEASUREMENT exists in R14.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/Mod/Import/DxfPlate/header14.rub | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/Mod/Import/DxfPlate/header14.rub b/src/Mod/Import/DxfPlate/header14.rub
index 17d05768a..ca0074928 100644
--- a/src/Mod/Import/DxfPlate/header14.rub
+++ b/src/Mod/Import/DxfPlate/header14.rub
@@ -35,6 +35,10 @@ $INSUNITS
  70
 4
   9
+$MEASUREMENT
+ 70
+1
+  9
 $PEXTMAX
  10
 50
-- 
2.43.0

